# 201 - Database Integrity Cleanup

**Phase:** 2 (Empty World)
**Effect:** Server starts clean, no FK constraint errors
**Status:** Completed (2026-04-02)

---

## The Effect

When creatures are deleted from the world, all related tables are cleaned up. No cascade errors, no orphaned references, no 50,000-line error logs.

The empty world is **truly empty**, not "empty with 50k warnings."

---

## What This Solved

### Before (Just Delete Creatures)

SQL script:
```sql
DELETE FROM creature WHERE id1 NOT IN (
    SELECT entry FROM creature_template WHERE type = 8  -- Critters
);
```

This deleted spawns but left references in:
- creature_addon (display/aura data)
- creature_formations (group movement)
- smart_scripts (AI behaviors)
- conditions (quest/spell triggers)
- waypoint_data (pathing)
- linked_respawn (respawn links)

**Result:** 50,000+ error lines on server start
```
SmartAIMgr::LoadSmartAIFromDB: Creature guid 153067 does not exist
creature_formations table leader guid 2891 incorrect
Creature (GUID: 489234) does not exist but has a record in creature_addon
...
(repeated thousands of times)
```

Errors.log: 4.8MB of warnings

### After (Cascade Cleanup)

Delete creatures AND cleanup:
```sql
-- Store keeper GUIDs
CREATE TABLE critter_guids AS
SELECT guid FROM creature WHERE id1 IN (
    SELECT entry FROM creature_template WHERE type = 8
);

-- Delete non-critters
DELETE FROM creature WHERE guid NOT IN (SELECT guid FROM critter_guids);

-- Clean up ALL related tables
DELETE FROM creature_addon WHERE guid NOT IN (SELECT guid FROM critter_guids);
DELETE FROM creature_formations WHERE leaderGUID NOT IN (...);
-- ... (6 more tables)

DROP TABLE critter_guids;
```

**Result:** 789 error lines (pre-existing upstream issues)

Errors.log: ~40KB (99% reduction)

